mtk-vcodec: decoder: accept standard V4L2 clients.

The vendor decoder reads v4l2_buffer.reserved on CAPTURE as a dma-buf fd
for a per-frame "general buffer" and treats only ~0 as "none". Standard
clients (FFmpeg, GStreamer) must zero reserved, so every capture buffer
failed with dma_buf_get(0) and REQBUFS/QBUF returned -EINVAL. Treat 0 as
"none" as well; Android's codec2 component never passes fd 0.

ENUM_FRAMESIZES for the coded formats reported the decoded-buffer
alignment (16x32) as a size step. Clients that honour steps reject
ordinary streams such as 1920x1080. Report the coded size range as
continuous; the driver pads decoded buffers to the alignment itself.

TRY_FMT/S_FMT on CAPTURE replaced an unsupported raw format (e.g. YU12)
with the vendor's compressed block format and reported success. FFmpeg
trusts that result and then reads every frame with the wrong layout.
Reject unsupported capture formats instead.

vpud's default UFO-compressed output (M2CS) has no standard equivalent.
With its uncompressed block layout (vpud property
vendor.mtk.vdec.frame.layout.mode=0) it produces M21S: 16x32-tiled NV12
with chroma directly after luma in one buffer, which vpud writes there
even when given a separate chroma plane. That is the layout standard
clients know as single-plane MM21 (GStreamer NV12_16L32S); present M21S
as MM21 and serve MM21 requests with M21S.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c
@@ -1223,7 +1223,9 @@
 				ctx->input_max_ts);
 		}
 	} else {
-		if (buf->reserved == 0xFFFFFFFF)
+		/* Standard V4L2 clients must zero reserved; only Android's
+		 * codec passes a general-buffer fd here (or ~0 for none). */
+		if (buf->reserved == 0xFFFFFFFF || buf->reserved == 0)
 			mtkbuf->general_user_fd = -1;
 		else
 			mtkbuf->general_user_fd = (int)buf->reserved;
@@ -1324,6 +1326,27 @@
 	default:
 		return v4l2_ctrl_subscribe_event(fh, sub);
 	}
+}
+
+/*
+ * vpud's uncompressed block output M21S is MediaTek's 16x32-tiled NV12 with
+ * the chroma plane directly after the luma plane in one buffer, which vpud
+ * writes regardless of the plane addresses it is given. Standard clients know
+ * this layout as single-plane MM21 (GStreamer NV12_16L32S), so present M21S
+ * as MM21 and serve MM21 requests with M21S. The vendor's own MM21 entry is
+ * a two-plane variant that vpud does not produce.
+ */
+static bool mtk_vdec_mm21_to_m21s(struct v4l2_format *f)
+{
+	if (f->fmt.pix_mp.pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT21)
+		return false;
+	f->fmt.pix_mp.pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT21S;
+	return true;
+}
+
+static u32 mtk_vdec_client_fourcc(u32 fourcc)
+{
+	return fourcc == V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT21S ? V4L2_PIX_FMT_MT21 : fourcc;
 }
 
